<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 4 July, from 1776 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1776 CE <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Continental Congress adopts the Declaration of Independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress approved the final text of the Declaration, drafted chiefly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a>. Its assertion that all men are created equal, with unalienable rights, became the founding statement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1802 CE <span class="tih-ago">224 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Military Academy opens at West Point</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Military Academy formally opened at West Point, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. It went on to train generations of officers, among them Grant, Lee, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> and MacArthur.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1826 CE <span class="tih-ago">200 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Adams and Thomas Jefferson die on the same day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Former presidents John Adams and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> died within hours of each other on the 50th anniversary of the Declaration. Adams's reported last words were 'Thomas Jefferson survives', unaware his rival had died first.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1863 CE <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vicksburg surrenders to Ulysses S. Grant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a 47-day siege, John Pemberton surrendered Vicksburg and nearly 30,000 men. With Port Hudson falling days later, the Union controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> and split the Confederacy in two.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 CE <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Polish leader Władysław Sikorski dies in a crash at Gibraltar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Sikorski, prime minister of the Polish government-in-exile, was killed when his aircraft crashed seconds after take-off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>. His death removed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>' most respected Polish voice at a critical moment.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 CE <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Philippines gains independence from the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> became a sovereign republic after nearly half a century of American rule, as promised by the 1934 Tydings-McDuffie Act. For decades 4 July was celebrated as its Independence Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1997 CE <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mars Pathfinder lands on Mars</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's Pathfinder bounced to a landing on airbags in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ares">Ares</a> Vallis and soon deployed Sojourner, the first rover on another planet. The mission returned thousands of images and revived public interest in Mars.</p></div></li></ol>
